<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Samora Machel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1933–1986</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Samora Machel was a Mozambican revolutionary who commanded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frelimo">FRELIMO</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> army and became its leader after Eduardo Mondlane's assassination in 1969. He was the first President of independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mozambique">Mozambique</a> from 1975, building a one-party socialist state while supporting liberation movements in Rhodesia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>. He died in 1986 when his aircraft crashed inside South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/samora-machel.jpg" alt="Samora Machel" width="320" height="422" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Department of Defense. American Forces Information Service. Defense Visual Information Center. 1994 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Samora_Moises_Machel_detail_DF-SC-88-01383.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
